Subject: [ZEROX] Smooth player join chunk work without dropping gameplay

- Starts joined players at a small send distance after PlayerJoinEvent and
  increases it one chunk at a time.
- Keeps Bukkit events and world mutations on the authoritative main thread.
- Feeds chunk loading/generation gradually into Paper's existing worker system.
- Bounds per-player chunk send/load/generation rates and concurrency.
- Serializes simultaneous join finalization to one player per tick.
- Reports slow synchronous event listeners with plugin, event and listener class.
- Never cancels, skips or replaces join work.
- Respects explicit post-join plugin changes to player send distance.
- Migrates only exact upstream Paper defaults and backs up paper-global.yml.
